From b533e3fb13c1bffe489dbeb45ddc481460709092 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:09:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(profiles): profile_config_scope binds the launch
 scope inside a bound scope

profile_config_scope(launch home) on a single-profile host unbound an
enclosing secondary with three legacy setters, ending in
set_terminal_scope(None). Inside a bound scope (bind_profile_scope, a scoped
turn) clearing the terminal policy always raises ScopeSwitchRefused, so
profile provisioning for the launch profile failed there.

With a scope bound, bind the launch profile whole instead: bind_state over
scope_for_profile(launch), launch secrets unstamped, terminal policy over the
LIVE TERMINAL_* env (not launch_terminal_env, which would freeze the launch
snapshot before multiplex activation). The no-scope and multiplex paths are
unchanged.

Reachability: kanban_db_dispatch's bind_profile_scope wraps only config/toolset
reads and the spawn-env build, which never reach profile_config_scope, so the
dispatcher does not hit this on main; it is latent for any caller that runs
provisioning inside a bound scope on a single-profile host.

Task: t_01a1d3eb07d8da1a
